WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.840
A small harbour.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.000
A depth marker on the wall
rises and falls with the tide.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.310
At high tide the water
is eight metres deep.

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.920
At low tide, just two metres.

5
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.610
A fishing boat needs at least
four metres of water under it.

6
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.640
Plot depth against time
and the tide traces a wave.

7
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.050
So when is the harbour
too shallow for the boat?

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.400
Only at the moment of low tide?

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.850
In this mission, you'll describe a
wave by its highest and lowest values,

10
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.190
its middle line, and the
time it takes to repeat.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.400
And you'll model it with
a sine or cosine graph:

12
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.720
amplitude, principal axis and period.

13
00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: work out when the
water is too shallow for the boat.
